Subject: [PATCH] provenance: re-key the ledgers for the v0.1.3.1 export

The export rewrite (mailmap, path/e-mail scrub, internal-material removal including the matching sections of historical patches/series blobs, fork range only) changed every fork sha, so the sha-pinned ledgers are re-keyed ONCE from the pre-rewrite originals via filter-repo's commit-map; pruned commits keep their original key with a sha_note. The base pin in sources.json is not re-keyed: the upstream base is byte-identical.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release engineering for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - audit tooling and ledgers only; no inference code path is touched.
